course: dictionary
lesson: 6900
title: Owe: money, favours and thanks
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Owe is a verb, so it changes: I owe, he owes, she owed, and owing. It has three main meanings. The first is money: when someone lends you money, you owe it back. «The family owes $12 for school lunches» means they must pay that money back.
explain: The second meaning is about what you must give or do for someone because of what they did. «I owe you a favour» means you will do something kind for them later. The third meaning is about thanks: «I owe my success to my coach» means my coach helped me to succeed.
explain: To check the meaning, swap in a simple phrase. Does «must pay back» fit? Does «must give back» fit? Does «because of» fit? If one of them makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: «Owe» means to have to pay back money that someone lent you.
fact: «Owe» can also mean you must give or do something for someone because of what they did.
fact: «Owing to» means because of, as in «owing to heavy rain».
fact: Debt is the money you still owe. To repay is to pay it back.
fact: Owe, owes, owed and owing are all forms of the same verb.
exercise: «Everett's family owes $12 for school lunches.» What does owes mean here? | They won a lunch prize | They are happy with the school | *They must pay back money | They have plenty of lunch to share
exercise: Maya says «I owe you one» after you help her. What does she mean? | *She will help you back one day | She owes you one dollar | She is angry with you | She has lost one of your things
exercise: Which word is the past tense of owe? | ownership | owing | *owed | owes
test: «I owe my success to my coach.» Which meaning is this? | *Something good happened because of someone's help | Borrowing a book | Paying back money | Saying sorry
test: «Owing to heavy rain, the match was cancelled.» What does owing to mean? | Owing money to | Without | Before | *Because of
exam: «A bet needs both people to agree; nobody owes anything for a deal they never accepted.» Why does nobody owe anything? | *They never agreed to the deal | The bet was a gift | They already paid everything | They are too young to bet
